    {
      "title": "Nvidia CEO reportedly targeted by Chinese spy",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/29/nvidia-ceo-targeted-chinese-spy",
      "description": "<p>Jensen Huang reported to have had close relationship with tech company executive suspected of passing intel to China</p><p>US intelligence agencies believe the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/nvidia\">Nvidia</a> chief executive, Jensen Huang, has been targeted by a Chinese spy who had done business with him, according to a <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/29/us/politics/nvidia-china-jensen-huang-trump.html\">new report</a> by the New York Times.</p><p>Alice Huang or Huang Le, of no relation to the Nvidia CEO, is an executive at a Singapore-based datacenter company called Megaspeed. She had previously been suspected of smuggling Nvidia chips to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/china\">China</a>, prompting American officials to surveil and monitor her. Those officials have determined that she was acting as a Chinese intelligence asset, passing commercial information to Beijing, the New York Times reported, citing unnamed sources.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/29/nvidia-ceo-targeted-chinese-spy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T15:23:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nvidia chief Jensen Huang reportedly targeted in Chinese spy plot",
